<a href="https://sportstalkcolumbus.podbean.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="SportsTalk Columbus Podcast" style="color: #0062B2; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;"><img class="govd_template_image" src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2020/05/3352385/podcast-icon-03_original.png" style="width: 560px; height: auto !important; max-height: auto !important; border: none;" alt="SportsTalk Columbus Episode 3" width="560" height="144"></a><a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/sportstalk-columbus-podcast/id1504940909?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="SportsTalk Columbus Podcast" style="color: #0062B2; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;"><img class="govd_template_image" src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2020/04/3285307/listen-on-apple_original.png" style="width: 163px; height: auto !important; max-height: auto !important; border: none;" alt="Apple Podcasts" width="163" height="35"></a><a href="https://open.spotify.com/show/26J47vJlHhu4k13LmswkKZ?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="SportsTalk Columbus Podcast" style="color: #0062B2; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;"><img class="govd_template_image" src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2020/04/3285311/listen-on-spotify_original.png" style="width: 104px; height: auto !important; max-height: auto !important; border: none;" alt="Spotify" width="104" height="41"></a><p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;"><br>In episode three of SportsTalk Columbus, Jack Castle sat down with Steve Baxter, Assistant Manager with Columbus Recreation and Parks Department, Sports Office. Currently, Steve manages the adult volleyball leagues and outdoor facilities rentals for the Sports Office but is proud to announce our latest program, Adult eSports. Listen to the podcast and learn more about this program and how and why Steve decided now is the best time.</p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">Episode Sponsor - <a href="https://roosterswings.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" title="Roosters" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Roosters</a></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;"><a href="http://crpdsports.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/SportsTalk-Columbus-Show-Notes-5-7-20.pdf?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" title="SportsTalk Columbus Podcast Show Notes" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Episode Show Notes</a></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;"><a href="http://crpdsports.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Columbus Recreation and Parks Sports Office</a></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">Intro and Exit Music: <a href="https://freemusicarchive.org/music/XTaKeRuX/The_way_iam/Rocking_Forward_?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Rocking Forward</a> by <a href="https://freemusicarchive.org/music/XTaKeRuX?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">XTaKeRuX</a> and is used under a <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">CC BY 4.0 International license</a>.</p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">We are proud to present SportsTalk Columbus, brought to you by the partnership between B.A.T.S. and Columbus Recreation and Parks Sports Office. Our mission is to engage with the Sports Community of Central Ohio off the field by being a leader in the sports community by providing insights and commentary by industry experts.</p>
